# dev-guardian (MCP)

This project has the dev-guardian MCP server registered. 54 tools and 18
resources for security, quality, bugfix, deps, compliance, observability,
performance, plus first-class WordPress and .NET (C#/F#) support. All
scanners run locally, no telemetry, results persisted in
`.guardian/guardian.db`.

**Prefer these MCP tools over invoking scanners directly** — you'd lose
diff_scans, baselines, suppressions, and the regression history.

## Intent → MCP tool

### Security
- "is this safe?" → `security_scan_full`
- "secrets?" → `scan_secrets`
- "CVEs?" → `scan_deps` / `deps_audit`
- "Dockerfile / container" → `scan_containers`
- "IaC" → `scan_iac`
- "deep bug hunt" → `bug_hunt`
- "what routes does this app expose?" → `map_attack_surface`
- "active DAST / pen-test the running app" → `map_attack_surface` then
  `scan_dast` (target app must already be running; loopback-only unless
  `authorized_target: true`; a clean result is not evidence of injection
  safety)
- "is this finding reachable?" → `map_attack_surface` then `validate_finding`
  (reachable/unreachable/unknown per finding, report-only; unreachable never
  available for Ruby/Java/C#/PHP — it IS produced, and can be wrong, for a
  CLI/cron/queue-only file or an unresolvable dynamic import)

